  "result": "I added `wrapText(text, width)` in `src/core/wrap.ts` and committed it as `51ffa1c`. `npm run fast` passed, including Biome, the boundary check, tsc and the related tests.\n\n- **Behavior:** It splits on any whitespace and joins words with single spaces. Words are never split unless one is longer than `width`, in which case it is cut into `width`-sized chunks. Empty or blank text returns `[]`. Widths below 1 are treated as 1.\n- **Helpers:** I reused nothing. Core may not import from other areas, and I found no existing wrapping helper in `src/`.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/wrap.test.ts` has four cases covering normal wrapping, exact-fit words, whitespace handling and over-long words. I added its entry to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs` with a weight of 0.1.\n- **Commit title:** No task id was in the brief, so the title has no `(<task id>)` suffix, which the repo convention requires. If you give me the id, I can amend the commit.",
